From 2bab13028986a06c439b739d2d37013c70464799 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zonglvye <zonglvye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:10:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 84/90] feat(qishui): run the Qishui client inside the shell

qishui-music-api is a Node package: it signs with P-256 and reads/writes Buffer,
and every call it makes has to go through a same-origin proxy because Qishui's
API carries no CORS headers. This lands the three pieces that make it runnable
in the WebView:

- qishuiNodeCrypto: Buffer + node:crypto on top of @noble/curves (synchronous,
  which the protocol requires). The DER it produces is byte-compatible with
  Node's: the CSR it builds verifies in openssl and Node verifies its signatures.
  vite aliases 'node:crypto' to it, so the upstream package stays unpatched.
- qishuiLocalApi: the account lives in localStorage (no electron-store here),
  and every fetch is rewritten into the shell proxy's query form.
- bootstrap imports it once, so the Buffer shim is installed before any call.

Verified on the device: window.__foliaQishui does a real search (3 tracks,
2.2 s), gets a playable source (preview=false, standard) and 2702 chars of krc
lyrics through the shell proxy.
